# Line endings
#
# Text files are normalised to LF in the repository; working trees keep their
# platform's native endings. Without this the same checkout disagrees with
# itself across environments: Windows git here runs core.autocrlf=true and
# stores LF while checking out CRLF, so a WSL git (which has no autocrlf) reads
# every text file as wholly modified.
* text=auto

# Kept explicit: these are text the detector could otherwise guess at.
*.svg text
*.toml text
*.lock text

# Never touched.
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
